In `vtora-ruka.js` I wrote the most important probe like this:

   if (pokritie === 0) {
     k(nezavisimo === null, "zero coverage → NOT MEASURED");
   }

Then I planted exactly the defect it was written against — the uncovered falling back onto my label. I expected it to fail.

MEASURED: it did not fail. With the defect the coverage becomes 158, the condition does not hold, and the probe SIMPLY DOES NOT RUN. 5 of 16 failed, and it was not among them. After the fix: 8 of 19.

⚠️ THE FORM, and why it is worse than an ordinary hole: the probe is silent EXACTLY WHEN the defect is present. Its condition depends on the same thing it judges. While the defect is absent, it is green and seems to protect; once it appears, it vanishes from the report.

FIXED: the empty case is supplied EXPLICITLY (`probvai({})`), the live state of the file is not read. The probe always runs.

The same family as B-132 from the same day — there the instrument measured "does it write DIFFERENTLY now" instead of "does it write". Here the probe asks "if the coverage IS zero" instead of "whatever the coverage". Both answer correctly for the state in which they are run, and wrongly for the question.
